      "dom_id": "question-52265",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that  $64-64w+16{w}^{2}=0$, find $w.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the left-hand side is a perfect square. It just needs to be factored:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64-64w+16{w}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {8}^{2}-2\\cdot 8\\cdot 4w+(4w)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (8-4w)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(8-4w)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{0} \\\\ |8-4w| & =0 \\\\ 8-4w & =0 \\\\ 4w & =8 \\\\ w & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
